  "$comment": "The materials look layer of #139 (GD ruling 15 Oct 2026, ticket 444): species under the 12 ore families. A species names its family, never a gate class (#142); family ids, ore ids and prices stay. pool is the species set a row belongs to (legacy = P1 and P2; a planet's pool is ores.economy.json kinds.pools, ticket 542) and slot the kind slot of ores.economy.json it binds to (TD ruling on ticket 446); a row's family, rarity and gradeBand equal its slot's. Hue slots: hue in degrees, saturation and luma in 0..1 (Rec. 601 display luma); a slot keeps out of the reserved hue bands of oreLooks.json and above the brightest host rock. gradeBand is the species' depth window, first and last band in 1..5. The legacy rows are Content's roster for ticket 447 (names cut to an epithet before the family name, flavour to one ledger sentence). The foothold rows (#453) fill every slot of kinds.mixed once per pool: foothold-p3, foothold-p4, foothold-p5 and foothold-p6-p7, 17 each, every species its own hue slot and silhouette + pattern pair; hero marks rare, epic and mythic for the follow-up hero art ticket.",
